  "summary": "Postinstall executes remote shell script from third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh | sh') (line 107), fetching and executing a shell script from a mutable master branch of the rtk-ai/rtk repository at install time. The script also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads os.homedir(), and branches on process.platform. The fetched install.sh comes from a mutable branch with no pinning, hash verification, or signature check, so the executed bytes can change at any time without a corresponding package release. The publisher scope (@leejungkiin) does not match the fetched repository owner (rtk-ai), and the package's declared purpose does not document remote shell execution as part of dependency management.",
